**Date:** 1 November 2026 · **Deciders:** greensteph, support desk

Replaces [0001 · Duplicates share a subject line](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).

## Context

[0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merged reports by subject line alone, so nobody read
the body. It was fast, but it put different bugs in one ticket. #4471 is the proof: 412 reports
merged as one "known" issue actually held two causes, the month-first parser (379) and the
`booking-v3` form hint (33). The second had no ticket of its own and no owner.

## Decision

Subject match still groups incoming reports, because it is fast during an incident. But before a
ticket goes to engineering, split it by **cause**, computed by `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` from the
tenant's locale and booking form, not by its subject. One cause, one ticket, one owner. A report
whose body reads differently from its computed cause (`desk-notes.json`) is footnoted, not hidden.

## Consequences

- #4471 splits into two tickets: the parser bug (379 reports) and the form-hint bug (33 reports).
- Engineering sees one thread per cause, with an honest count, instead of one ticket of 412.
- Triage stays fast: the subject-line group is still the first pass; the cause split runs on the
  merged set, from data, at render time.

